    seed_per_call_env_rebuild_o_globals_regression_2026-08-21, 0, "2026-11-27 p3sweep-20261127: CowEnv (e73a0bec647) fixed the callee-side attach, but publish_and_repoint still walks the caller nonlocal_overlay superset 3x per call (publish_live_bound_globals, drop_published_globals, mark_published_globals_refreshed) and module-top-level frames note EVERY declared global into that superset, so calls from module-level code pay 3xO(module globals) for zero publishes. Measured on fresh HEAD seed: per-call wall 1.3us at 0 globals vs 213us at 4096 (160x); SIMPLE_PERF_COUNTERS PUBLISH_GLOBALS_SCANNED=205,200,000 (1026/call) with PUBLISHED=0 across 200k calls. Fix (patch applied in worktree, NOT built): publish_candidate_entries/len/names = dirty_names UNION refreshed_globals with the same is_local/overlay filters (src/compiler_rust/compiler/src/value.rs); the five publish/refresh/sync consumers switched to candidates (interpreter_call/core/function_exec.rs); counter semantics documented (perf_counters.rs). Equivalence: every overlay insertion records dirty or refreshed; the sole neither-recording insertion (restore_frame_owned) only holds frame-owned names because take_frame_owned refuses shared-bound keys; all consumers require a global binding - so candidates == superset after the consumers' filters, consumers verified idempotent for the write-then-refresh double-yield case. Re-verification recipe: rebuild seed, scaling probe expect per-call ~flat across N; counters expect SCANNED ~2/call vs NONLOCAL superset by design; SIMPLE_LIB=src sh scripts/check/check-lint-cost-budget.shs --fixture src/compiler/80.driver/driver_types.spl --budget 240; cargo test -p simple-compiler value_tests. Doc projection noted: the 60s gate may stay RED even with the O(globals) term removed (interpreted body cost dominates - separate documented work). close_evidence reproducer=build/p3cache/envrebuild/probe_1024.spl prevention=test/01_unit/compiler/interpreter/env_scope_bucket_hoist_contract_spec.spl"

